meta {
  name: Release Stock
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/inventory/release
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{adminAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "items": [
      {
        "skuCode": "{{productId}}",
        "quantity": 1
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Compensating action for Reserve Stock.bru (InventoryRepository.increment) — best
  effort, no check that the item was ever actually reserved. In production
  order-service calls this from its own catch block if persisting the order fails
  after inventory was already decremented (see OrderService.createOrder — the comment
  about the remote reserve() transaction already having committed).

  Same ROLE_ADMIN-via-gateway quirk as Reserve Stock.bru.

  Expected: 204 No Content, always (no 404/409 path — incrementing a skuCode that
  doesn't exist just matches zero rows silently).
}
